I'm in the process of updating my Slash'EM spoiler on Demogorgon (see
http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/slashem/demogorgon.html), and I
wonder if anyone could help me work out the details.  Although the
spoiler is for Slash'EM, I believe that Demogorgon is much the same in
vanilla Nethack.

The question I'm trying to answer is:

How many rounds can you go against Demogorgon before you need to stop
and heal yourself?

Reasonable assumptions to make:
* You are very fast and unburdened, although Demogorgon may have cast
  haste self.
* You are able to cast cure sickness at 0% failure.

In the old version of Slash'EM (based on Nethack 3.3.1), you had to
heal yourself whenever you were ill, because Demogorgon might get four
sickness attacks against you in a single round.  Now he can only get
two sickness attacks in, and then only when he gets two moves in a row
against you.

The confusing bit is that although I know that Demogorgon's first
sickness attack will leave you with between 20 and (19 + Con) turns to
live, and each subsequent attack will divide your time to live by 3
(rounding down) and then add 1, I'm not clear on how many moves the
player or Demogorgon will get during a "turn".  I asked for help with
this once before (see
http://groups.google.com/groups?hl=en&lr=&ie=UTF-8&oe=UTF-8&selm=xo24ruvkgnh.fsf%40tcm16.phy.cam.ac.uk)
but none of the replies really explained how it worked.
